From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] motor: let devres free the device

thingino fix for #1351, regenerated as a continuation diff for the
pinned vintage source layout (common/misc/motor): motor_probe()
allocates mdev with devm_kzalloc() but the probe error path and
motor_remove() also kfree() it, so devres frees the device a second
time - kernel heap corruption on failed probe and on module
unload/reload. The ms419xx copy of the same pattern is not touched
here (not built for this board).

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
  1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)
--- a/common/misc/motor/motor.c
+++ b/common/misc/motor/motor.c
@@ -995,7 +995,6 @@ error_min_gpio:
 		del_timer_sync(&motor->min_timer);
 		del_timer_sync(&motor->max_timer);
 	}
-	kfree(mdev);
 error_devm_kzalloc:
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -1046,7 +1045,6 @@ static int motor_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	misc_deregister(&mdev->misc_dev);
 
-	kfree(mdev);
 	return 0;
 }
 
